<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Livonia</h1><p class="st-meta">1570 CE – 1578 CE · capital Oberpahlen</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Puppet kingdom created by Ivan the Terrible for the Danish prince Magnus during the Livonian War, which collapsed within eight years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV of Russia</a>, seeking to win the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-germans">Baltic Germans</a> to his side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>, proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-duke-of-holstein">Magnus of Holstein</a>, brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-denmark">Frederick II of Denmark</a> and ruler of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/danish-osel">Danish Ösel</a>, king of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-confederation">Livonia</a> in 1570. Magnus was to rule all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> as the tsar's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, and he married Ivan's relative <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-vladimirovna-staritskaya">Maria Staritskaya</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-duke-of-holstein">Magnus</a> resided at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poltsamaa">Oberpahlen</a> (Põltsamaa) in central <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>. His kingdom depended entirely on Russian troops and never controlled the major towns. A 30-week siege of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a> in 1570-1571 failed, and the Estonian and Livonian nobility largely refused to accept him.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1577 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-duke-of-holstein">Magnus</a> tried to act independently and was punished by Ivan, who seized his towns. Magnus fled to Polish protection in 1578, renounced his royal title and died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piltene">Pilten</a> in 1583. The kingdom disappeared, and its lands were divided among Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-livonia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Livonia" width="320" height="287"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LIVONIAE_NOVA_DESCRIPTIO_1573-1578.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1570 CE – 1578 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Oberpahlen</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Magnus of Livonia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Estonia, Latvia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Livonian Kingdom</dd></dl></aside></div>

